# Impact of Social Networking Sites and Digital Applications upon Teens

**Authors:** Roehl, Amy, Stewart, Alyssa Humphries

## Abstract
This review of literature focuses on youth development by examining the effects of use of social networking sites and digital applications on teens.Recent research demonstrates that using these types of digital media amplifies existing issues teens face, contributes to new concerns, and affords new opportunities. In order to navigate this relatively new digital communications landscape, adults in the family and broader community must be informed about the issues, engage in conversation with teens about digital media use, and model healthy behavior.

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ1209116

